But hold on — is `waitForScreen(RegExp('•{15}'))` a "transient exact-count anchor" again, the very class of flake the PR set out to kill? No — the original flake was waiting for an intermediate count (5 of 15) on the raw stream; the screen never goes "backwards" — bullets only get added as you type, and the final state has exactly 15. Waiting for the FINAL property on the painted screen is a proper synchronization point (it's the terminal state, monotone: once 15 bullets are painted, they stay). The value row never loses bullets. So waiting for the full 15-bullet row on screen is sound.

But there's subtlety: after Enter/submit, sheet closes — but we wait before Enter. Fine.

However: `waitForScreen` doc says the returned screen is the FIRST frame containing the pattern (no settle). For asserting the bullet count on the captured screen, first frame containing 15 bullets — the value row on that frame has ≥15 bul…

