  "body": "Follow-up to gh-1244 / PR #1245 (review thread next step).\n\nPR #1245 converted `test/integration/secret_sheet_test.dart` to the `typeSecret` property anchor (full N-bullet row on the painted screen via `waitForScreen` + the `maskedValueRow` `│`-guard helper in `test/integration/pty_harness.dart`; race-free raw-transcript security scan). The same exact-transient `waitForText('•••••')` anchor — the flake class that red-led main run 37232401938 — still exists at 5 sites:\n\n- `test/integration/secret_sheet_residual_test.dart` — 4 sites (lines ~92, ~120, ~181, ~219)\n- `test/integration/password_prompt_pty_test.dart` — 1 site (line ~56)\n\nSame failure mode: the wait pins an intermediate bullet count on the raw stream, so the PTY can paint past the checkpoint before the 50 ms poll evaluates (and the focused row's cursor cell is wrapped in inverse-video escapes, so N consecutive `•` need never exist in the stream at all).\n\n## Fix\n\nConvert each site to the same property anchor introduced in PR #1245 (`harness.waitForScreen('•' * secret.length)` + `maskedValueRow` on the anchored screen + the raw-transcript plaintext scan), keeping the surrounding test intent (frame-intact checks, paste scenarios, grant/decline flows) unchanged.\n\n## AC\n\n- AC1: no `waitForText('•••••')` (exact transient bullet count) remains in `test/integration/`.\n- AC2: affected files green across repeated CI runs of the PTY leg."
}
